# Environment

Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. **Never commit `.env.local`** — it is already
in `.gitignore`. Every variable here is optional: the site builds and runs without
them, it just has no catalogue and an inert admin.

```
# --- Supabase (required for the catalogue and the admin) ---
# Project URL and anon key: Dashboard → Project Settings → API
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<anon public key>

# --- Instagram ---
# This is the same as the built-in default, so it can be left out entirely.
VITE_INSTAGRAM_URL=https://www.instagram.com/bags_daily.ph/

# --- Contact ---
VITE_CONTACT_EMAIL=cycybaranda@gmail.com

# --- Analytics (leave unset to stay completely inert) ---
VITE_ANALYTICS_URL=https://plausible.io/js/script.js
VITE_ANALYTICS_DOMAIN=your-domain.example
```

## Which keys are safe to expose

`VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` is **designed to be public** — it ships in the bundle
whenever you build. It identifies the project, not you. Every permission in this
app is enforced by Row Level Security in Postgres, so a tampered client gets
exactly the same access as a well-behaved one.

The **service-role key must never appear in anything under `src/`**. Nothing here
needs it: the browser reads and writes through RLS. If you ever find yourself
adding a server route that uses the service-role key, that is a signal you need a
server, not a client.
